      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Augmented reality: a virtual cube on a planar marker\n\n1. cv2.findChessboardCorners detects the board's 9x6 inner corners (the IMAGE points) and reports whether the board was found.\n2. 'CV Grid Points' builds the matching flat 9x6 grid of OBJECT points (z=0 plane), and 'CV Camera Matrix' supplies approximate intrinsics (fx=fy=image width, principal point = image center - good enough for a near-frontal board; calibrate with 'Calibrate Camera' for accuracy).\n3. 'Solve PnP (Pose)' recovers the board's rotation + translation. It is failure-tolerant: no board -> found=false, zero pose.\n4. A virtual cube ('CV Points', 3D, z negative = up out of the board) is projected with cv2.projectPoints and drawn as a single polyline through its 12 edges ('Draw Polygon', open).\n5. Basic data handling 'if/else' gates the overlay on 'found': an image without a board passes through unchanged.\n\nInspect the recovered pose (rvec/tvec) as text. Object and image points MUST be in the same order - 'CV Grid Points' is row-major to match findChessboardCorners."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
